:: Walk to the backyard {"position":"150,200","size":"100,100"}
Jam’s mission to pick up the delivery was simple: follow the sun-drenched pavement path around to the back of the resort. But the plan was pleasantly hijacked halfway there.

Sprawled across a broad, flat stone like some prehistoric king holding court, was a lizard. A huge one. It was utterly motionless, a statue carved from sun-warmed stone and dappled scales, soaking in the morning light with a calm that felt ancient.

Jam stopped, instantly charmed. The world seemed to slow. In the quiet, blissful repose of its sunbathing, the lizard's face—with its heavy-lidded eyes and noble profile—seemed to hold the faintest, wisest of smiles. It was a masterclass in stillness, and for a moment, Jam forgot all about the ticking clock and the melting smoothies waiting up the path.

[[Feed the lizard]]
[[Got scared, ran away]]
[[Ignore the lizard, go back to the apartment building]]



